  "A fan in a D-shaped duct (flat side down): very strong static thrust, falling off quickly with airspeed. Air only.": "A fan in a D-shaped duct (flat side down): very strong static thrust, falling off quickly with airspeed. Air only.",
  "A fan in a square duct: very strong static thrust, falling off quickly with airspeed. Air only.": "A fan in a square duct: very strong static thrust, falling off quickly with airspeed. Air only.",
  "A fan in an octagonal duct: very strong static thrust, falling off quickly with airspeed. Air only.": "A fan in an octagonal duct: very strong static thrust, falling off quickly with airspeed. Air only.",
  "A hinged flap: aileron, elevator, rudder - whichever way it is placed. Moves with the pilot's steering.": "A hinged flap: aileron, elevator, rudder - whichever way it is placed. Moves with the pilot's steering.",
  "A main rotor: lift with the up / down thrust (collective), the cyclic steers with your controls. Its torque turns the ship the other way: counter it with a reversible rotor mounted sideways away from the centre, or gyros. Its thrust is limited to what your ship can hold against that torque. Air only.": "A main rotor: lift with the up / down thrust (collective), the cyclic steers with your controls. Its torque turns the ship the other way: counter it with a reversible rotor mounted sideways away from the centre, or gyros. Its thrust is limited to what your ship can hold against that torque. Air only.",
  "A propeller on a turbine: strong static thrust that falls off with airspeed (constant power). Air only.": "A propeller on a turbine: strong static thrust that falls off with airspeed (constant power). Air only.",
  "A small rotor that thrusts forward or backward along its axis. It answers your movement and your rotation controls, like any thruster, but either way. Air only.": "A small rotor that thrusts forward or backward along its axis. It answers your movement and your rotation controls, like any thruster, but either way. Air only.",
